{"name":"Senate","hex":"#4a515f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Senate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of several legislative bodies.","The council that governed the ancient Roman Republic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Senate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Senate","blocks":[{"text":"A senate is a deliberative assembly, often the upper house or chamber of a bicameral legislature. The name comes from the ancient Roman Senate, so-called as an assembly of the senior and therefore considered wiser and more experienced members of the society or ruling class. However the Roman Senate was not the ancestor or predecessor of modern parliamentarism in any sense, because the Roman senate was not a de jure legislative body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Cicero_Denounces_Catiline_in_the_Roman_Senate_by_Cesare_Maccari.png/330px-Cicero_Denounces_Catiline_in_the_Roman_Senate_by_Cesare_Maccari.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senate"},{"title":"Senate (France)","blocks":[{"text":"The Senate is the upper house of the French Parliament, with the lower house being the National Assembly, the two houses constituting the legislature of France. It is made up of 348 senators elected by part of the country's local councillors in indirect elections. Senators have six-year terms, with half of the seats up for election every three years. They represent France's departments (328), overseas collectivities (8) and citizens abroad (12)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/French_Senate_Logo.svg/330px-French_Senate_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senate_(France)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Senat_2833.jpg/500px-Senat_2833.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Senat_2833.jpg/1280px-Senat_2833.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Senat_2833.jpg/500px-Senat_2833.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The debating chamber of the Senate of the Czech Republic in the Wallenstein Palace","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASenat_2833.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Senate_in_session.jpg/500px-Senate_in_session.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Senate_in_session.jpg/1280px-Senate_in_session.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Senate_in_session.jpg/500px-Senate_in_session.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Senate of the United States in session","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASenate_in_session.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg/500px-S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg/1280px-S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg/500px-S%C3%A9nat-4_%2847547673571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS%C3%A9nat-4_(47547673571).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t